{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 20,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Part of this video is sponsored by LastPass.\nMore about LastPass at the end of the show."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5000,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a video about research into slowing the rate of aging"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9900,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and extending the human lifespan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12180,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, before I filmed this I wanted to know:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15080,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What do you guys generally think about such research?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18340,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I made a Twitter poll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19860,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where I found that the majority of people were supportive and thought there should be more of it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24180,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there were some important concerns and I want to address those here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27300,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the beginning. I mean the most significant concern was:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30420,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if we're looking to extend human lifespan,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32500,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "does that just mean we'll have more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34620,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sick years where we'll be in bed with Alzheimer's?\nNobody wants that, and that was clear to me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40240,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the professor that I was interviewing for this video, professor David Sinclair, points out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45100,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that as you get older the risk of horrible diseases, things like diabetes and cancer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52020,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and arthritis, all those sorts of things... it increases exponentially."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56940,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, if this research is successful the whole point of it will be to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62900,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "forestall those sorts of diseases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64820,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, if you really are tackling aging,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68060,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you should also see that those age-related diseases do not set in so quickly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73780,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, the point of slowing aging and extending human lifespan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78240,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is to extend the healthy lifespan, also called the health span."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83680,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The other concerns I saw were that people were saying:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86580,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Well, this could be used only for the wealthy and increase inequality\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89940,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or \"It could increase the population of the Earth causing...\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93560,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"...more garbage, more CO2. Where are the resources to feed all these people?\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97400,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think these are valid concerns, but they're not part of the scope of this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102260,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you want to discuss them in the comments, feel free, but the point of this video is to address:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107280,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can we slow aging in humans? Can we extend the lifespan and the health span?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112940,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what does that look like? How do we do it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115800,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay. So for this video I traveled up to the 'Bodega Marine Lab',"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120140,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is north of San Francisco and there I got to see some 'moon jellyfish'."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125740,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now what's fascinating about these 'moon jellyfishes' is that some people consider them immortal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131080,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How can that be?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132440,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So all these jellyfish have this complex life cycle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135760,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where they start off as a polyp,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138340,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is basically like a small sea anemone and then they'll go through a metamorphosis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142100,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and become a medusa. And the medusa stage is what we generally think of when we think about a jellyfish."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147100,
    "dDurationMs": 6700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in most of these species the polyps are generally able to asexually reproduce,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153840,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they can regenerate if tissue is cut off of them or if they're damaged,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158660,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they don't have any clear evidence of senescence, which is the term for biological aging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164960,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they appear to have some degree of immortality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167820,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No one had reported their ability to do this until... I think this was 2015."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172880,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So do 'moon jellyfish' hold the key to slowing aging and extending our lifespan?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178260,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Could they help us live forever?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180400,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before I got into making this video, I would have put this sort of research in the same category as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187380,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "downloading your brain, your consciousness into a computer. Like, I can see how maybe that would work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193840,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I don't think we're anywhere near that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196500,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because we don't even understand how the brain works or how memories are stored,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199260,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that seems like serious science fiction, so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202460,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would have put, say, extending the human lifespan to 120, 150, and beyond in the same category,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208180,
    "dDurationMs": 5740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but after reading professor Sinclair's book and doing an interview with him,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213920,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think it seems much more possible and in fact plausible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218080,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we'll make some progress over controlling aging in our lifetimes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222600,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, if you want to slow aging, the first question you need to answer is:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227720,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why do we age in the first place? I mean, what really is aging?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232120,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've made a video in the past about telomeres."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234840,
    "dDurationMs": 6940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are the end caps on your chromosomes. And every time a cell divides the telomere gets a bit shorter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241780,
    "dDurationMs": 1820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it was thought that these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243620,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "telomeres are kind of like the tips of your shoelaces and they prevent the chromosome from fraying."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there are other signs in older bodies that you have old cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254480,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are an accumulation of things, they're called senescent cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257620,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're essentially these zombie-like cells that just go on living in your body and inflaming the cells around them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264120,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's poor intercellular communication,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268020,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's mitochondrial dysfunction, those are the powerhouses of the cell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271440,
    "dDurationMs": 7320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are these 8 or 9 different features of older cells and they are the hallmarks of aging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278800,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the question is: are they the cause of aging,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282260,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or are they kind of the result of a deeper root cause?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286580,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the middle of the last century, the hypothesis was that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290980,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was damage to our DNA, mutations to our DNA that happened over  the course of our lives"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295860,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that led us to be older"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298500,
    "dDurationMs": 860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299820,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "evidence since then has suggested that that is not really the case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303720,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, you can take an adult cell,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306800,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you can clone it into a new organism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311340,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that organism appears to live about as long as non-cloned organisms of the same species."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317860,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the first sheep, Dolly the sheep, had a short lifespan. She died early."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322360,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But cloned animals; you can now clone a monkey,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325100,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can clone dogs, in fact Barbra Streisand, the actress, she cloned her dogs,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329920,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they are expected to live a normal lifespan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332320,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in that way it seems like all the information is still there in the DNA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336780,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if we're not losing information in our DNA then what is the reason for aging?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343220,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, professor Sinclair suspects that it's a loss of information,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347040,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but not the information in our DNA, in our genome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351420,
    "dDurationMs": 6260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, professor Sinclair suspects that the loss of information is in our epigenome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357960,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what is the epigenome?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360340,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every cell in your body has the same DNA,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364900,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but, different cell types have different epigenomes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368760,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have different ways of packaging that DNA,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371820,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coiling up, you know, a lot of it so that it's not read,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375360,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and leaving some parts of the DNA spooled out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378240,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's easier to transcribe and turn into proteins and run that cell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383220,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the epigenome is responsible for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385800,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turning on or turning off different parts of the DNA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390140,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The way it does that is with proteins called 'histones'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393500,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that, essentially, the DNA is wrapped on,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397040,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and also things like methylation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399360,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So there's these chemical signaling markers which are placed on the DNA in certain positions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404940,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the idea is: when your body is first forming, the epigenome is what tells your cells what type of cell to be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412780,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as you get older,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414780,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "professor Sinclair's hypothesis is that we are losing information in the epigenome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419960,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's important because if a skin cell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422080,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "needs to remain a skin cell, that's the epigenome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426060,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you don't have the epigenome"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428220,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the skin cell will forget what type of cell it is and it might turn into a brain cell,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432140,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which may not be that bad but if your brain turns into a skin cell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435260,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you've got a problem and I think that's largely what aging is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438500,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've gotta say, there's some weird, hair patches, on my shoulder,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442780,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that have happened as I've gotten older."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444580,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is that a cell... doing the wrong thing?\nAre those meant to be skin cells?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449040,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Are they're screwing up or is this just some... I don't know."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452380,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, no, weird stuff happens when you get older, right?\nYou start to get hair growing where it shouldn't:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457940,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ears, nose, back.\nThat's cells losing their identity, the cells go:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463140,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I can't remember what I'm supposed to do, I'm not reading the right genes anymore.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466740,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, the key to this sort of breakdown in the epigenome"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471480,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is DNA damage?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474280,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, so when you go out in the sun, not like today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477180,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but on a day where there's a lot of sun, you'll break your chromosomes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480780,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in the effort that the cells go to to stick the chromosome back together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485120,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "note: the DNA isn't just flailing around, it's actually bundled up. The cell has to unwrap it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490240,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "recruit proteins to help,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492560,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "join it together, and then they have to go back and reset the structures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496500,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that resetting of the epigenome"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499160,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "happens about 99%. That 1% is the aging process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506420,
    "dDurationMs": 8020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So overtime, histones are not returned to the right places and DNA methylation is added in places where it shouldn't be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515300,
    "dDurationMs": 7640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can read that methylation pattern and I could tell you how old you are, exactly, and when you're even gonna die."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523960,
    "dDurationMs": 1540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How could you tell that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525520,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, it's a clock, we call it the Horvath clock named after my good friend Steve Horvath,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529560,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so these little chemicals that accumulate on the DNA like a plaque on the teeth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533680,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can read that and the more you have, the older you are; biologically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537920,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you might only be 40,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539400,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're younger than 40, of course but, you know, I'm 50 now,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543180,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I might be biologically 60, actually I was."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546520,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I changed my life and then the test said I was biologically 31."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550400,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, one of the things I found really interesting was: you found a way to make mice age faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556560,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, how did you do that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557740,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the clock of aging is due to the loss of the information in the cell,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562160,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and one way to accelerate that is to go break a chromosome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565580,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of going in the sun we engineered a mouse where we could break its chromosomes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569420,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not enough to cause mutations, the cells put the DNA back together, so we didn't lose any genetic information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575680,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if we're right about the 'epigenetic information theory of aging',"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579680,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those mice should get old and that's exactly what happened."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583300,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's gray, it's got a hunchback,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584980,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's got dementia, all its organs look old,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587720,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the real test was: \"what if we measured that DNA clock?\" what we call the 'DNA methylation clock'."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594200,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we measured it and those mice were actually 50% older than mice that we didn't treat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599720,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that isn't just a mouse that looks old, that mouse literally is older."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604700,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's interesting about this hypothesis is that, if it's true,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607980,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if the noise accumulating the epigenome is really what's causing aging,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612860,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well then there are steps we can take right now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616400,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to slow the rate of aging in our bodies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619240,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by trying to better maintain our epigenomes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622440,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do we do that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625760,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's this theory, that billions of years ago"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629200,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "early bacteria took an important evolutionary step."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632840,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They actually developed two different modes of living."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636800,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When times were good they used their energy to grow and reproduce."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640980,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when conditions were tough, they used their energy to protect and repair their cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646520,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They evolved, what professor Sinclair calls: 'longevity genes'."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650380,
    "dDurationMs": 7260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These genes triggered by adversity create enzymes which among other things, maintain the epigenome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657640,
    "dDurationMs": 6020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And today, those same longevity genes can be found in bacteria, and us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663720,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have these 'hormetic response' genes or 'longevity genes' that are in all of our cells,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667920,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they sense when we've run a lot, we've lost our breath or we're hungry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671840,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we are a little bit hot, or a little bit cold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674260,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These genes are turning on our general defenses against aging. So, what is that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678120,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, parts of our cells fall apart: they can put them back together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681920,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Proteins misfold: they can get rid of them or put them back together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685800,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The ends of the chromosomes get shorter: they can lengthen them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688420,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lot of processes that go on but one of the most important, I think,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692040,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is maintaining the information, the epigenetic information in the cell,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695740,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that our cells don't forget what to do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699960,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are three types of longevity gene."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702040,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are the ones we work on called 'sirtuins' and they control the information in the cell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706420,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, 'sir' in sirtuin stands for 'silent information regulator' number two (SIR2)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711820,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are other ones. The other group is called AMP-kinase or AMPK."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716540,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This group of genes senses how much energy we're taking in... mostly in the form of sugar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721960,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then the third group is called mTOR."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724220,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And these genes control and respond to how much amino acids we're taking in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729400,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you eat a giant steak, you've got a lot of amino acids coming into your body."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734480,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That'll actually prevent mTOR from hunkering down and keeping you being longer lived."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739580,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the mouse experiments actually bear this out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742300,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The best way to make a mouse live longer is to reduce the amount of time it eats,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747920,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so periodic fasting, intermittent fasting,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751280,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to keep it a little bit cool,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753620,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to restrict its amino acids."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756260,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the recipe for long life for a mouse, and it's true for monkeys as well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760140,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that have been calorie restricted studies where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762500,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these monkeys for 15 years didn't eat as much food as the ones that gorged themselves whenever they wanted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767160,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they were protected. They didn't just age slower."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770160,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They didn't get as much diabetes and heart disease, they were actually fit and healthy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774160,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when the control group, eating whatever they wanted, aged and became sick quicker."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778460,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When some people think about eating less,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like, calorie restriction as a way to extend their life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784960,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That doesn't seem like a very pleasant way to extend life. I mean, to be hungry for longer..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790620,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So are there other ways to... you know, mimic that effect? Or to simulate that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796120,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are these molecules that turn on the sirtuin pathway,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800460,
    "dDurationMs": 6900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and trick the body. And so, for example, in the lab if I give some of our mice a molecule called 'NMN',"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807420,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which raises the level of a chemical called 'NAD',"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811520,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get hyperactive defenses in the body."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814320,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what did you see in these... 'senescent mice' that you gave NMN to?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819200,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we had a bit of an incident. These mice that we gave NMN to ran 50% further,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824980,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but actually some of them ran so far that the machine, the little treadmill, stopped working."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829600,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we had to reprogram the software"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831500,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because this program had never seen a mouse that ran more than three kilometers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835980,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Three kilometers for a mouse?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838320,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For an old mouse. They outran the young mice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841100,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's like an ultramarathon for us?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843340,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That would be probably like taking a 70 year-old and making them run faster than a 20 year-old; further."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850380,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, so these are ultra marathoners,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852380,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if we did that to humans I imagine you could have 90 year-olds winning Olympic medals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857740,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to sum up, there are six things that you can do right now to slow the rate of your aging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 863040,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Starting with zero: avoid DNA damage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866280,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wear sunscreen, avoid x-rays and all that sort of stuff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869460,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number one: eat less. Caloric restriction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872940,
    "dDurationMs": 6700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number two: eat less protein, because your body has ways of detecting how much of that you're taking in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879640,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number three: do some exercise.\n'High-intensity interval training' (HIIT)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883060,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Get your heart rate up to 85%, make your body feel like you're running from a lion or something."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887820,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number four: be uncomfortably cold,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 890760,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or number five: be uncomfortably hot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894380,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of these things will trigger your body's 'longevity genes' into maintaining your epigenome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901900,
    "dDurationMs": 6100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Going into 'repair and protect mode' rather than 'grow and reproduce', and if you think about those things,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908000,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those are generally all the things that we don't do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911040,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what if slowing aging isn't enough for you?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914780,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, this is where my interview with professor Sinclair took an interesting turn,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918640,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because he's actually done some research on reversing aging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923420,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how would you do that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925320,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, effectively, you would need to take the epigenome and reset it back to an earlier time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931140,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how is that possible?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932980,
    "dDurationMs": 7660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Back in 2012, a scientist named Yamanaka received the Nobel Prize for discovering four factors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940640,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which when applied in a gene therapy to an adult cell,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944620,
    "dDurationMs": 6020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would reset the whole epigenome back to how that cell was when it was an embryo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950640,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it is what is called a 'pluripotent stem cell'."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954540,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, you wouldn't want to apply that to your entire body because,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958360,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, then you would turn into a giant tumor because your cells wouldn't know how to differentiate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963280,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it does suggest that there are ways of resetting your epigenome,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968120,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they could be the key to reversing aging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970880,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The big breakthrough that we just had in my lab,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973800,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "finally, you know, about a year or so ago,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975820,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was to reprogram the eye of a mouse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979460,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the eye, we chose the eye because that's a very hard thing to fix, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983460,
    "dDurationMs": 3239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you go blind when you're older, we think that's a one-way thing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 986700,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're never going to recover your vision,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988960,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we decided: let's try it anyway, let's go for broke."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992260,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we put our gene therapy in the eye of old mice,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995260,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turn their retinas to be young again, reversed aging in their retinas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999760,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So those one-year old mice went back to about two months,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1003180,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And guess what? Those mice could see again, just like they were young again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1007140,
    "dDurationMs": 6340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How do you reset one of these eye cells without resetting it to just a stem cell?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013480,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we have to be very careful not to reset these cells to be basically a stem cell,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019120,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "otherwise, we wouldn't have mice that can see, we'd have mice with a giant tumor in the back of their eyes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024240,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what we do is a couple of things:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026200,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we didn't use all of the four reprogramming factors that won the Nobel Prize, we use just three,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031160,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we leave off one called 'cMyc', which causes cancer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034120,
    "dDurationMs": 7380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and those three seem to be just the right recipe for taking the age of the eye backwards, but not too far."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041500,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, the second thing we do is: we turn it off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043740,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can actually turn this system 'on' when we want, and 'off' again,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047360,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that we don't take them too far back in age."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050340,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can you do that with any cell?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052340,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We think we can do this in any tissue. We've now given it to the whole mouse and those mice are fine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057440,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No evidence of cancer. They seem to be really quite healthy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060640,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the big question is: can you take a mouse way back, the whole body, and be totally younger?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066600,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe back from two years, back to two months. And that's what we're doing right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071600,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's pretty exciting!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073559,
    "dDurationMs": 2681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's freakishly exciting, actually!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1076240,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I thought we'd just slow down aging, now we're talking about an aging reset."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079540,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know what? We've only reset the age of the eye once,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083060,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how many times can we do this? Maybe it's twice. Maybe it's a hundred times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1087520,
    "dDurationMs": 7340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, professor Sinclair claims that his gene therapy reversed aging in the mouse's eye and allowed it to see again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094880,
    "dDurationMs": 6980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But applying a gene therapy to every one of your trillion cells is pretty impossible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1101900,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in order for this to actually work and reset an entire body,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106740,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you would need another way, and this is where the jellyfish come in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1111480,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because 'moon jellyfish'—any cell in an adult jellyfish can actually be reset"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117520,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into an earlier stage of its life cycle. It can become a polyp again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122920,
    "dDurationMs": 7300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it seems like the jellyfish are actually capable of activating something like the Yamanaka factors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1130220,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and resetting their epigenomes to an earlier time in their lives."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134760,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we were able to figure out how they do that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1137140,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, then maybe we could do the same with our own cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1141220,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We do have the ability to reset our epigenomes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144500,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that is typically only used when we're in the embryonic stage,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1148580,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when we need to maintain all our cells as stem cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1151580,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As we age, most mammals including humans,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1154760,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we lose stem cells over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156860,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the stem cells we do have become more and more restricted over time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1160320,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the types of cells they can make."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1162500,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if we can understand how the 'moon jellyfish' can take, presumably, many different kinds of cells,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1169000,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and reverse-engineer them into the cells it needs during regeneration,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173340,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that might give us an idea of how to do it in ourselves, as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1176480,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, I still think we're a fair ways off from reversing aging in the entire human body."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1183160,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what I found interesting from talking to professor Sinclair was that there's at least a roadmap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1188520,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At least a path ahead where you can see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1191440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it could be possible to slow and even reverse aging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1200400,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey this part of the video is sponsored by LastPass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1203700,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's talk about one thing you can do right now to improve your life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1207660,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just go to LastPass.com and start a free account and enjoy free cross-device sync."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1212940,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think about how spending just a few moments right now could save you hours or even days"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1217740,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the course of your life and that's because you will never again get locked out of an account."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1222280,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'll never have to reset a password"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1224280,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'll no longer have to burden your brain with remembering passwords or end up having to write them down,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229860,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it will make your passwords more secure, because LastPass auto-generates strong passwords for you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1235100,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I love how it auto-fills usernames and passwords on websites,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1239180,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it works just as well on iOS or Android apps and mobile sites."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1243480,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just think about how much hassle and time this will save you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247120,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you end up living to, like, a hundred or a hundred and twenty."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1250540,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean how many accounts and passwords will you even have by then?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1254190,
    "dDurationMs": 5809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you want extra features, like 'advanced multi-factor authentication', you can upgrade to LastPass premium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260070,
    "dDurationMs": 3739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So put your passwords on autopilot right now with LastPass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1263809,
    "dDurationMs": 5051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Click on the link below to find out more and thanks to LastPass for sponsoring this part of the video."
    } ]
  } ]
}
